{
  "auth_detail": "Authorization: token <api_key>:<api_secret> (a dedicated Helpdesk agent user, role Agent) · in-cluster http://frappe.example.com:8000 needs no Host header; when config.site_host is set the runner also sends Host: <site_host> (multi-site benches routed by Host)",
  "auth_kind": "api_key_header",
  "auth_params": {
    "header": "Authorization",
    "value_template": "token {{secret.api_key}}:{{secret.api_secret}}"
  },
  "credential_schema": [
    {
      "hint": "User settings → API access → Generate keys",
      "label": "API key",
      "name": "api_key",
      "secret": true
    },
    {
      "hint": "shown once, when the keys are generated",
      "label": "API secret",
      "name": "api_secret",
      "secret": true
    },
    {
      "hint": "only when the site name differs from the base URL host",
      "label": "Site host (optional)",
      "name": "site_host",
      "secret": false
    }
  ],
  "description": "HD Ticket create/read and internal agent comments over the Frappe REST API (/api/resource), verified live against Frappe 15.123.1 + Helpdesk 1.31.0 (B7 T16, 2026-10-21). raised_by is the customer when case.create gets customer_email (Helpdesk accepts an unknown email and creates no Contact), else the service user env.requester_id. Idempotency needs a unique custom field on HD Ticket (fieldname custom_agent_key); a second insert with the same key answers HTTP 417 UniqueValidationError, which maps to invalid_input (the dup_search before the insert is what prevents it). case.comment writes an HD Ticket Comment: internal, not a customer-visible reply (Helpdesk replies go through hd_ticket.reply_via_agent). Helpdesk 1.31 ships the statuses Open, Replied, Resolved and Closed; Paused is mapped for sites that add it. Basic auth (key:secret) is accepted as well as token.",
  "key": "frappe_helpdesk",
  "label": "Frappe Helpdesk",
